# Copy to .env — it is not committed — and fill in what applies.
#
# The deployed site's database. With this set, `npm run dev`, `npm start` and
# `npm run admin` all run on the same accounts and the same saved work as the
# site: one copy, nothing to keep in step. Vercel's Neon integration writes the
# same string into the project's environment, so this is that string.
#
#   Vercel › the project › Storage › Neon › .env.local  (or Neon's dashboard)
#
# POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require
#
# To work on this machine's own SQLite file instead, for one run:
#   scripts/dev.sh --local

# The account the development server signs in as, with no password, from this
# machine and the Wi-Fi it is on. Empty stops at the sign-in page.
# HANZI_DEV_USER=admin

# A natural voice for reading Mandarin aloud, if you have an Azure Speech key.
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=
